<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Henry Craig</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1748">1748</a>–<a href="/years/1812">1812</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Sir James Henry Craig</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir James Henry Craig was a British general who commanded the troops that, with Admiral Elphinstone's fleet, took the Cape from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> in 1795, and he governed the colony until 1797. He later served in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and was governor general of British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> from 1807 to 1811.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-henry-craig.jpg" alt="James Henry Craig" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Lawrence · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:James_Henry_Craig_1806.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
